# What never enters the build context.
#
# Two different jobs, and only one of them is about speed.
#
# 1. Correctness. `.venv/` is a virtualenv built against the *host* — on a
#    developer's machine that is Windows or macOS, with platform-specific
#    wheels and absolute paths baked into its scripts. Copied into a Linux
#    image it shadows the one the build produced and fails in ways that read as
#    dependency problems. The same is true of every `node_modules/`.
#
# 2. Disclosure. Everything sent to the daemon can end up in a layer, and a
#    layer is not deleted by a later `RUN rm` — it is still in the image
#    history for anyone who pulls it. `.env` files, keys and `.git/` (which
#    holds every secret ever committed and reverted) must not be sent at all.
#
# Deny-list rather than allow-list, deliberately. An allow-list is safer for
# disclosure and worse for correctness here: the build needs several scattered
# paths across a monorepo, and the failure mode of forgetting one is a build
# that breaks loudly. The failure mode of forgetting a deny entry is a secret
# in a published layer, so the entries below err toward over-excluding.

# -- Correctness: host-built artefacts that must not shadow the image's --------
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/.open-next/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# -- Disclosure ---------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/service-account*.json

# -- Caches and local state: large, useless in an image, sometimes revealing ---
.turbo/
**/.turbo/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.pnpm-store/
htmlcov/
coverage/
.coverage
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
pgdata/
*.log

# -- Not part of the runtime image --------------------------------------------
#
# Tests are excluded because they are not copied by the Dockerfile anyway, and
# leaving them in the context invites a future COPY that puts a test runner's
# fixtures — including any credentials a test fixture grows — into production.
apps/api/tests/
apps/web/
docs/
md/
infra/
scripts/
services/
packages/
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
*.md
